    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **256 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the change so that creating an owner returns a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nThe DTOs are generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec, and the model\u2192DTO mapping runs through MapStruct, so the change lives in three places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` property (readOnly `string`) to the `Owner` response schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `displayName` field that flows out to the JSON response of every owner endpoint, including the `201 Created` returned by `addOwner`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Mapped `displayName` via an expression backed by a helper:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(formatDisplayName(owner))\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n\n   default String formatDisplayName(Owner owner) {\n       if (owner == null) return null;\n       return owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName();\n   }\n   ```\n   The format is derived from the *stored* names (`getLastName()`/`getFirstName()`), so it reflects the persisted values after the controller's normalization.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 Added `createOwnerReturnsDisplayName`, asserting the create response contains `\"displayName\": \"Franklin, George\"` for a `George Franklin` owner.\n\nBecause the mapping lives in the shared `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, `displayName` is populated consistently on create as well as on the get/list responses, with no change needed to the controllers.",
